APPENDIX 2 <Amended on Nov. 5, 2019>
Enforcement Decree of the Act on the Assignment and Operation of Responsible Administrative Agencies in the Military
Appointment Authority over Civilian Military Employees of Responsible Administrative Agencies in the Military Delegated to Heads of Agencies (related to Article 21)

Agency category | Appointment authority delegated to the head of the agency

1. A responsible administrative agency in the military headed by a general-grade officer of the rank of major general or higher, or by a Class I fixed-term general civilian military employee.
(a) Authority to transfer Class II general civilian military employees (excluding general-type fixed-term general civilian military employees).
(b) Authority to appoint general civilian military employees of Class III or lower (excluding general-type fixed-term general civilian military employees) and specialist civilian military career officers of corresponding rank.
(c) Authority to appoint general-type fixed-term general civilian military employees of Class III or lower and specialist fixed-term general civilian military employees and temporary fixed-term general civilian military employees of corresponding rank.

2. A responsible administrative agency in the military headed by a brigadier general or a Class II fixed-term general civilian military employee.
(a) Authority to transfer Class III general civilian military employees (excluding general-type fixed-term general civilian military employees).
(b) Authority to appoint general civilian military employees of Class IV or lower (excluding general-type fixed-term general civilian military employees) and specialist civilian military career officers of corresponding rank.
(c) Authority to appoint general-type fixed-term general civilian military employees of Class IV or lower and specialist fixed-term general civilian military employees and temporary fixed-term general civilian military employees of corresponding rank.

3. A responsible administrative agency in the military headed by a colonel or a Class III fixed-term general civilian military employee.
(a) Authority to transfer Class IV general civilian military employees (excluding general-type fixed-term general civilian military employees).
(b) Authority to appoint general civilian military employees of Class V or lower (excluding general-type fixed-term general civilian military employees) and specialist civilian military career officers of corresponding rank.
(c) Authority to appoint general-type fixed-term general civilian military employees of Class V or lower and specialist fixed-term general civilian military employees and temporary fixed-term general civilian military employees of corresponding rank.

4. A responsible administrative agency in the military headed by a lieutenant colonel or a Class IV fixed-term general civilian military employee.
(a) Authority to transfer Class V general civilian military employees (excluding general-type fixed-term general civilian military employees).
(b) Authority to appoint general civilian military employees of Class VI or lower (excluding general-type fixed-term general civilian military employees) and specialist civilian military career officers of corresponding rank.
(c) Authority to appoint general-type fixed-term general civilian military employees of Class VI or lower and specialist fixed-term general civilian military employees and temporary fixed-term general civilian military employees of corresponding rank.
